                    "text": "The Supreme Court's initial obstruction of Education Department layoffs was judicial overreach\u2014halting necessary reforms to redirect resources from bloated bureaucracy to actual classrooms. The Big Beautiful Bill proves America First priorities: cutting administrative bloat while protecting Pell Grants (+7% funding in H.R.1) and increasing state education control by 22%.\n\nCisneros confuses trimming fat with cutting muscle\u2014real stupidity is letting 40% of Title I funds get devoured by administrative overhead instead of reaching students.\n\nThis restructuring finally forces D.C. to stop laundering taxpayer money through redundant middlemen and return authority to local districts where it belongs.",
