                    "text": "The ACA's subsidy cliff was always unsustainable\u2014forcing taxpayers to prop up premiums instead of fixing systemic cost drivers. A 60-year-old couple paying $13k more proves the system's broken, not that subsidies should be permanent.\n\nReal reform requires slashing hospital monopolies, drug middlemen, and bureaucratic bloat\u2014not endless cash infusions into a flawed structure. When DC claims \"affordability\" hinges on temporary credits, it's admitting their model failed.\n\nTime to scrap the Band-Aids and rebuild healthcare around price transparency, not subsidy addiction.",
